# MCP client protocol support and Durable Object fallback

## Decision

Serve **both eras, with a sunset note**:

1. Send `2026-07-28` requests directly to the stateless Effect Worker handler.
2. Send legacy `initialize` and `Mcp-Session-Id` traffic to one named Durable Object that owns one long-lived Effect stateful runtime.
3. Publish legacy support as temporary. Remove it after all named first-party clients negotiate `2026-07-28` by default and production telemetry shows less than 1% legacy traffic for 30 days, with at least 90 days' notice.

Do not put modern traffic behind the Durable Object. It would add an extra hop and serialize traffic that Effect and MCP deliberately made stateless.

Modern-only is too early on 2026-09-21. Claude Code reaches `2026-07-28` over direct HTTP, but Cursor, Pi's installed MCP adapter, Codex, MCP Inspector, and the v1 TypeScript SDK still negotiate a 2025 revision by default.

## What changed in MCP `2026-07-28`

The current protocol removed the initialization lifecycle and protocol sessions, including `Mcp-Session-Id`. Each request carries protocol version, client identity, and capabilities in `_meta`; `server/discover` provides optional up-front discovery. This is why Effect can implement `McpProtocol.v2026_07_28` without a session map. Source: [MCP `2026-07-28` changelog](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/changelog), read 2026-09-21.

## Client matrix

“Default against HTTP” is the deployment-relevant column for `https://ratstack.sh/mcp`. Local probes used a server that accepted both eras and recorded the first request. Probe artifacts remain under `/tmp`; the relevant wire facts are copied below so the result does not depend on those temporary files.

| Client checked on 2026-09-21 | Default against HTTP | Newest available today | Evidence and confidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Claude Code `2.1.278` | `2026-07-28` | `2026-07-28` | **Verified locally.** `/tmp/mcp-http-probe-claude.jsonl` begins with `server/discover`, `Mcp-Protocol-Version: 2026-07-28`, and matching `_meta`; later `tools/list` uses the same revision. Direct stdio still opened with `initialize` at `2025-11-25` in `/tmp/mcp-probe-claude.jsonl`, so transport matters. Independent remote-connector evidence: [anthropics/claude-code#93290](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/93290). |
| Claude Desktop `2.2553.1` installed locally | `2026-07-28` for a claude.ai remote connector | `2026-07-28` | **Externally observed; this exact local build was not wire-probed.** [anthropics/claude-code#93290](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/93290), opened 2026-09-10, records Claude for Mac sending `2026-07-28` request metadata through a custom connector. [#94806](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/94806), opened 2026-09-16, records the Cowork desktop MCP client negotiating `2026-07-28`. Treat local stdio servers separately until directly tested. |
| Pi package `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` `0.86.1` plus installed `pi-mcp-adapter` `2.34.0` | `2025-11-25` | `2026-07-28`, only when the server config explicitly sets `protocolVersion: "auto"` or `"2026-07-28"` | **Verified from installed source.** Pi core intentionally has no MCP client: `node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/usage.md` (“does not include built-in MCP”). The extension's `~/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-mcp-adapter/types.ts` says the default is `"legacy"`; `server-manager.ts` maps `"auto"` and `"2026-07-28"` to SDK v2 negotiation. Its installed `@modelcontextprotocol/client` `2.0.0` proposes `2025-11-25` in legacy mode. |
| Codex CLI `0.155.0` | `2025-06-18` | `2026-07-28`, behind an under-development feature and, for stdio, a server opt-in | **Verified locally and in source.** `/tmp/mcp-probe-codex.jsonl` records `initialize.params.protocolVersion: "2025-06-18"`. [`protocol_mode.rs`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/rmcp-client/src/protocol_mode.rs) makes `Legacy` the default and proposes `2025-06-18`; [`features/src/lib.rs`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/features/src/lib.rs) marks `mcp_2026_07_28` under development and disabled by default. |
| Cursor Agent `2026.09.18-9a7762b` | `2025-11-25` | No verified `2026-07-28` mode | **Verified locally.** `/tmp/mcp-http-probe-cursor.jsonl` records `initialize` at `2025-11-25`, then `Mcp-Session-Id` and `Mcp-Protocol-Version: 2025-11-25` on later HTTP calls. `/tmp/mcp-probe.jsonl` records the same revision over stdio. No current source or documented switch proving modern negotiation was found; modern support is therefore unverified. |
| MCP Inspector source `2.7.0` | `2025-11-25` | `2026-07-28` when `protocolEra` is `"auto"` or `"modern"` | **Verified from current source.** [`package.json`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/blob/main/package.json) pins `@modelcontextprotocol/client` `2.0.0`. [`core/mcp/types.ts`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/blob/main/core/mcp/types.ts) defines modern as `2026-07-28` but says an omitted era means legacy `2025-11-25`; [`clients/cli/src/cli.ts`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/blob/main/clients/cli/src/cli.ts) exposes `--protocol-era legacy|auto|modern` and says ad-hoc targets otherwise default to legacy. |
